    "notes": [
      "Hardware mode: FLT, DEMP and FMT low (normal latency filter, no de-emphasis, I2S); SCK to ground uses the internal PLL from BCK (3-wire I2S: BCK, LRCK, DIN).",
      "XSMT high to play: a pull-up to 3.3 V (10 kΩ) or a GPIO; pulling it low before power is removed avoids a pop.",
      "The outputs are ground-centred (charge pump): no DC-blocking capacitors; the 470 Ω + 2.2 nF RC on each output filters out-of-band noise.",
      "Separate AGND and DGND near the part, joined under it on one ground plane."
    ],
    "page": "Figure 33 simplified schematic, hardware-controlled subsystem; 10.1.1.2; 11.1 power supply pin descriptions"
  },
  "notes": [
    "PCM5101A (lower SNR) and PCM5100A share the pinout. All digital inputs are failsafe Schmitt-trigger inputs: 3.3 V I2S from an ESP32 or a Pi works directly."
  ],
